      "locator": "Printed87 prose below the explanatory grid, through printed88 first paragraph.",
      "paraphrase": "Ready italic correction columns are built from a row-average correction times digits 1-9, rounded to integers in last-place units when tabular differences vary little. When they vary more, use parts of a row or calculate the full correction.",
      "applicability": ["why_direct_final_rounding_need_not_match_table_process"],
